FILE: vUX-progressIndicator.js
FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON
addEvents() bound 'online', 'offline' and 'transitionend' to window as anonymous
closures. All three were unremovable, and the tinyIncrement() setInterval was only ever
cleared by hideProgress() — an indicator torn down mid-progress kept the interval
running and kept writing to an element that had been removed. The three handlers are now
named, every element a progress block is built into is recorded, and destroy() clears the
interval, stops the grid animation, detaches the listeners and removes the injected
blocks.

The grid animation is now ended with the CShapes animation object's new destroy() rather
than stop(), so the canvas is cleared as well as halted.

